 structure into a  one-dimensional structure  then we're going to apply a unary  operation  less than zero to our one-dimensional  data structure which is called a vector  in apl and that's going to give us a  boolean vector of ones and zeros and  then we're just going to do a plus  reduce which is basically a sum  on uh the ones that corresponded to  negative numbers so  as an example you can imagine we have a  two by two matrix negative two  negative one zero and one and then if we  call  our algorithm on this uh plus reduce  zero  greater than uh ravel mat  you can see the first thing that happens  is we flatten our 2d  matrix into a one-dimensional vector  then we  call the zero greater than unary  operation and this  because this apl is an array programming  language this unary operation applies to  the whole vector  so it turns our negative numbers into  ones and our positive numbers into zeros  and then we just do our plus reduce  which is basically summing up all the  values in this boolean vector which  gives us two  so the last thing to talk about is the  time complexity for all of these  solutions which is going to be  linear in the number of elements in your  matrix or in other words it's going to  be big o of n  times n if n is the length of your rows  and m  is the number of columns as always if  you enjoyed this video and found it  helpful  hit that like button if you want to see  more make sure to hit that subscribe  button  you can follow me on twitter for  reminders 30 minutes before contests  start  and you can find all of the code shown  in my videos on my github page  thanks for watching and i'll see you in  the next video

